  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies on zone-level correlations from a single transit line expansion to suggest broader generalizability.",
      "what": "Using a difference-in-differences approach within a multiplicative framework, this study measures how the expansion of Rome's Metro C line affected local businesses. The analysis reveals a statistically significant increase in the total number of economic activities near the new stations, accompanied by a mild decline in economic diversity that points to spatial clustering. A focused analysis of microenterprises, which make up the majority of the dataset, tracks the associated shifts in local employment and GDP.",
      "why": "It provides empirical evidence that major transit investments generate positive economic spillovers at the neighborhood level, establishing a quantifiable correlation between accessibility gains and microenterprise growth that can help project the economic impacts of future transit lines."
    }
